  "notes": "The process of killing bacteria and microorganisms. Used in medical, food safety, and hygiene contexts.\n\nCOMPOUND: {殺|さつ} (kill) + {菌|きん} (bacteria)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {殺菌|さっきん}する: to sterilize\n- {殺菌|さっきん}{効果|こうか}: sterilization effect\n- {殺菌|さっきん}{作用|さよう}: antibacterial action\n- {殺菌|さっきん}{処理|しょり}: sterilization treatment\n- {加熱|かねつ}{殺菌|さっきん}: heat sterilization\n\nRELATED HYGIENE TERMS (in order of strength):\n- {除菌|じょきん}: germ removal (weakest — removes but doesn't necessarily kill)\n- {殺菌|さっきん}: sterilization (kills bacteria)\n- {消毒|しょうどく}: disinfection (reduces pathogens to safe levels)\n- {滅菌|めっきん}: complete sterilization (destroys all microorganisms)\n- {抗菌|こうきん}: antibacterial (prevents bacterial growth)",
